WEBVTT

00:00:00.654 --> 00:00:03.300
International Public Schools October 3

00:00:03.704 --> 00:00:07.678
Year 5A presents: The Space Tourism Agency.

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:09.508
A project by Mohamed,

00:00:09.528 --> 00:00:13.163
Bolous, Justin, Zeyad and Yassin.

00:00:13.654 --> 00:00:16.030
Under the supervision and guidance of Mr.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.022
Mohamed El Sayed, Mrs.

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:20.093
Rania Mamdouh and Mrs.

00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:21.235
Aliaa Salah.

00:00:23.408 --> 00:00:24.403
MBJZY

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:27.554
Space Group is a visionary space hospitality

00:00:27.574 --> 00:00:29.218
and tourism enterprise,

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:31.630
dedicated to building a greater tomorrow

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.755
beyond Earth, with a flagship orbital dome

00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:37.929
resort positioned near the giant planet Jupiter.

00:00:38.483 --> 00:00:41.653
The project brings together futuristic architectural

00:00:41.673 --> 00:00:44.827
engineering, sustainable life-support systems,

00:00:44.954 --> 00:00:48.095
and high-end resort living in deep space.

00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:50.975
At the heart of the concept is a monumental

00:00:50.995 --> 00:00:52.508
orbital dome station,

00:00:52.648 --> 00:00:55.871
suspended above planetary clouds and ringed

00:00:55.891 --> 00:00:58.957
cosmic horizons, designed to welcome travelers

00:00:58.977 --> 00:01:02.472
seeking both awe-inspiring scientific discovery

00:01:02.492 --> 00:01:04.083
and five-star comfort,

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.412
far from Earth.

00:01:05.903 --> 00:01:08.799
Every element of the project connects space

00:01:08.819 --> 00:01:11.729
exploration with practical travel details,

00:01:11.749 --> 00:01:13.236
visual storytelling,

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:15.111
and complete hospitality planning.

00:01:15.765 --> 00:01:18.727
The brand identity is anchored by a bold

00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:22.008
emblem, a golden orbital swoosh,

00:01:22.028 --> 00:01:25.390
and the tagline: Building a Greater Tomorrow...

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:26.523
Beyond Earth.

00:01:26.703 --> 00:01:29.691
While the flagship orbital dome hotel rises

00:01:29.711 --> 00:01:32.447
against Jupiter's swirling storms,

00:01:32.614 --> 00:01:33.987
atmospheric bands,

00:01:34.007 --> 00:01:35.312
and dramatic lighting.

00:01:35.803 --> 00:01:38.661
A geodesic glass-and-steel dome crowns the

00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:41.379
station, housing lush greenery,

00:01:41.402 --> 00:01:44.012
trees, illuminated walkways,

00:01:44.032 --> 00:01:46.001
and multi-tier living levels,

00:01:46.142 --> 00:01:48.856
while an expansive circular ring and structural

00:01:48.876 --> 00:01:51.991
hub beneath the dome support station operations,

00:01:52.027 --> 00:01:54.543
docking zones, and viewing decks.

00:01:55.034 --> 00:01:58.425
Surrounding planetary views feature Jupiter's

00:01:58.445 --> 00:02:01.720
iconic storms alongside distant moons and

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.806
cosmic light, and the visual identity blends

00:02:04.826 --> 00:02:07.397
sleek dark navy backgrounds with gleaming

00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:10.102
gold and crisp white typography,

00:02:10.281 --> 00:02:11.563
for a prestigious,

00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:12.875
futuristic look.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.716
Rather than treating space travel as bare

00:02:15.736 --> 00:02:18.932
survival, the project frames orbital life

00:02:18.952 --> 00:02:21.094
as a refined, comfortable,

00:02:21.114 --> 00:02:22.549
and memorable getaway,

00:02:22.754 --> 00:02:25.221
that bridges imagination and presentation

00:02:25.241 --> 00:02:28.099
structure by pairing visual scenes with clear

00:02:28.119 --> 00:02:31.338
tiers, pricing, and promotional offers.

00:02:32.292 --> 00:02:34.381
To accommodate different budgets,

00:02:34.401 --> 00:02:37.047
group sizes, and trip lengths,

00:02:37.188 --> 00:02:40.032
the resort organizes guest stays into clear

00:02:40.052 --> 00:02:42.689
accommodation tiers that create a natural

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:44.000
ladder of luxury.

00:02:44.504 --> 00:02:47.076
Special Dome Rooms offer an intimate,

00:02:47.096 --> 00:02:48.960
stylish orbital retreat,

00:02:49.114 --> 00:02:52.697
priced at $250,000 for a 7-day stay,

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.797
featuring warm wood accents,

00:02:54.817 --> 00:02:56.486
soft recessed lighting,

00:02:56.705 --> 00:02:57.918
a comfortable bed,

00:02:58.176 --> 00:03:00.653
a tidy workspace or seating area,

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:03.664
and a curved window framing sweeping views

00:03:03.684 --> 00:03:04.468
of Jupiter.

00:03:04.972 --> 00:03:07.908
Luxury Celestial Suites elevate the experience

00:03:07.928 --> 00:03:11.550
at $750,000 for a 14-day stay,

00:03:11.743 --> 00:03:14.132
offering more spacious interiors,

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:16.615
plush lounge seating with a round table,

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:19.522
refined finishes, and a wide observation

00:03:19.542 --> 00:03:22.400
window looking out toward Jupiter and neighboring

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.751
celestial bodies.

00:03:24.242 --> 00:03:26.540
At the pinnacle of orbital living,

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.784
Celestial Villas are priced at $1,450,000

00:03:30.804 --> 00:03:32.448
for a 14-day stay,

00:03:32.588 --> 00:03:35.377
and feature expansive multi-level layouts,

00:03:35.531 --> 00:03:37.034
curved glass walls,

00:03:37.054 --> 00:03:38.880
panoramic views of Jupiter,

00:03:38.903 --> 00:03:40.446
generous lounge areas,

00:03:40.466 --> 00:03:42.838
dining spaces, indoor greenery,

00:03:42.979 --> 00:03:45.146
a sweeping spiral staircase,

00:03:45.166 --> 00:03:46.953
and an upper-level sleeping loft.

00:03:47.457 --> 00:03:50.211
Placing all three tiers side by side makes

00:03:50.231 --> 00:03:52.737
it effortless for audiences or prospective

00:03:52.757 --> 00:03:54.595
guests to compare space,

00:03:54.619 --> 00:03:56.965
view scale, and stay duration,

00:03:57.132 --> 00:03:58.085
at a glance.

00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:01.285
Getting to the resort and gearing up for

00:04:01.305 --> 00:04:04.432
deep-space travel are presented as tangible,

00:04:04.573 --> 00:04:06.984
structured parts of the itinerary,

00:04:07.216 --> 00:04:09.289
rather than abstract concepts.

00:04:09.793 --> 00:04:13.198
Rocket Travel Offers highlight sleek spacecraft

00:04:13.218 --> 00:04:16.085
launching above planetary horizons,

00:04:16.147 --> 00:04:19.187
with glowing thrusters and MBJZY

00:04:19.207 --> 00:04:23.832
branding, offering round-trip travel at $180,000,

00:04:23.973 --> 00:04:26.974
alongside a 15% off discount for groups of

00:04:26.994 --> 00:04:28.819
four or more travelers.

00:04:29.323 --> 00:04:32.285
Our Uniforms showcases tailored space attire

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:35.719
in crisp white and deep navy with gold trim

00:04:35.886 --> 00:04:37.233
and MBJZY

00:04:37.253 --> 00:04:40.228
Space Group markings giving travelers practical

00:04:40.248 --> 00:04:43.974
flexibility with a $35,000 suit rental option

00:04:44.154 --> 00:04:47.220
or a $120,000 custom purchase that comes

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.896
free with VIP

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.643
Complementing transport and gear,

00:04:51.835 --> 00:04:54.511
Tickets Offers features sleek dark-and-gold

00:04:54.531 --> 00:04:57.255
boarding passes with clear pricing tiers:

00:04:57.512 --> 00:04:59.898
$250,000 for Special,

00:04:59.947 --> 00:05:02.372
$750,000 for Luxury,

00:05:02.512 --> 00:05:05.158
$450,000 for two guests,

00:05:05.182 --> 00:05:08.544
and $650,000 for three guests.

00:05:09.498 --> 00:05:11.796
Hospitality aboard the station shines through

00:05:11.816 --> 00:05:14.868
the Grand Open Buffet and Food Offers on

00:05:14.888 --> 00:05:17.612
Deck 05, where warm lighting,

00:05:17.649 --> 00:05:20.103
attentive chefs, dining tables,

00:05:20.123 --> 00:05:22.925
and tall curved windows looking out at Jupiter

00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:26.145
and its moons, frame an all-inclusive fine-dining

00:05:26.165 --> 00:05:27.079
atmosphere.

00:05:27.609 --> 00:05:31.313
Food offer pricing lists $15,000 per week

00:05:31.333 --> 00:05:32.716
for gourmet dining,

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:35.919
alongside a free All-Inclusive option,

00:05:36.098 --> 00:05:38.575
and a prominent menu board for Celestia Prime,

00:05:38.768 --> 00:05:40.059
Grand Open Buffet,

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.136
organizes the culinary spread into five distinct

00:05:43.156 --> 00:05:44.083
stations.

00:05:44.537 --> 00:05:46.626
The Seafood and Raw Bar features chilled

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:49.422
lobster tails, Alaskan king crab,

00:05:49.576 --> 00:05:51.457
fresh oysters on crushed ice,

00:05:51.477 --> 00:05:54.618
and tuna, salmon, and octopus sashimi;

00:05:54.972 --> 00:05:57.582
the Carving Station offers slow-roasted prime

00:05:57.602 --> 00:06:00.404
rib of beef, herb-crusted rack of lamb,

00:06:00.571 --> 00:06:03.347
and crispy roasted duck with orange glaze;

00:06:03.701 --> 00:06:06.806
Hot Entrées and Specialties include pan-seared

00:06:06.826 --> 00:06:08.769
sea bass with lemon herb butter,

00:06:08.792 --> 00:06:11.438
truffle wild mushroom tagliatelle,

00:06:11.566 --> 00:06:13.730
slow-braised wagyu short ribs,

00:06:13.766 --> 00:06:15.995
and roasted Mediterranean vegetables;

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.376
Biosphere Harvest and Appetizers highlight

00:06:19.396 --> 00:06:23.045
fresh hydroponic greens and micro-herb salad,

00:06:23.238 --> 00:06:26.495
artisan European cheese and charcuterie boards,

00:06:26.649 --> 00:06:29.012
and traditional baked pastries and artisan

00:06:29.032 --> 00:06:29.842
breads;

00:06:30.209 --> 00:06:32.936
and Celestial Desserts round out the feast,

00:06:32.956 --> 00:06:35.749
with orbit chocolate soufflé and macaron

00:06:35.769 --> 00:06:38.766
tower, exotic planetary fruit cascade,

00:06:38.894 --> 00:06:41.644
and warm berry tart with vanilla bean gelato,

00:06:41.784 --> 00:06:44.118
with all beverages and refreshments included.

00:06:44.772 --> 00:06:47.786
Alongside dining, Our Amenities showcases

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:50.025
sunlit indoor garden spaces,

00:06:50.045 --> 00:06:51.965
water features, trees,

00:06:51.985 --> 00:06:53.268
glass dome ceilings,

00:06:53.288 --> 00:06:55.898
and lounge areas, noting that the Biosphere

00:06:55.918 --> 00:06:58.134
and Zero-G Spa is included,

00:06:58.444 --> 00:07:02.808
while a VIP Deck upgrade is an extra $25,000.

00:07:03.763 --> 00:07:06.008
All of these visual assets and commercial

00:07:06.028 --> 00:07:09.224
details come together in a vertical three-by-four

00:07:09.244 --> 00:07:11.998
